60,3,1,talk,Minato,,"I think the Wetland Restoration is risky. The ground is clay, and the heat is high.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,May,,The Woodland Walk is expensive to maintain. The Market Plaza is not funded by the habitat fund.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Shizue,,The Sports Terraces are hard surfaces. They are easier to keep clean and safe.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Victoria,,The Sports Terraces fit the volunteer group that referees the youth league. It is a good match.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,The Sports Terraces use the hard ground where people already walk. It is practical.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@Shunichi, I agree. The hard ground is safer for the diggers too.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,May,,"@Victoria, the volunteer match is a strong point. It reduces the need for paid staff.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@May, the hard surfaces are cheaper to maintain. That is a good thing for the city.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Shizue, yes. The apron outside the hall was patched, but it is still usable. It is durable.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Minato, the phasing notes say we can keep the park open if we do the south first.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Minato,,I am leaning towards the Sports Terraces. It seems the most feasible given the ground conditions.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,May,,I am also leaning towards the Sports Terraces. The maintenance costs are lower than the woodland.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Shizue,,I agree. The Sports Terraces are simple and robust. They will last longer.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Victoria,,I support the Sports Terraces. It aligns with the existing volunteer efforts and staff capacity.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,I vote for the Sports Terraces. It respects the traffic patterns and the ground constraints.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Minato,,I think we have a consensus. The Sports Terraces are the best fit for our current situation.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,May,,Agreed. It is the most financially sustainable option in the long run.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Shizue,,I am happy with this choice. It is practical and considerate of the community.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Victoria,,I am confident in this decision. It is a rational choice based on the data.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,Let us proceed with the vote. I believe the Sports Terraces will serve the city well.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
